cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  GRIP: Joint Tyre-Wear and Wheel-Alignment Estimation from a
  Single Rolling Pass over a Ground-Embedded Optical Sensor
message: >-
  If you use this software or the GRIP-Roll dataset, please cite it
  using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shanmukesh
    email: shanmukeshbonal4622@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Shanmuk4622/tyre-wear-alignment-cv'
abstract: >-
  GRIP (Ground-level Rolling Inspection Pipeline) estimates tyre tread
  depth, wear-pattern class, and wheel alignment angles from a single
  pass of a vehicle over a ground-embedded optical sensor. A camera
  below a glass plate images the tyre contact patch, which is
  instantaneously stationary under the rolling-without-slip constraint
  and therefore free of motion blur at any vehicle speed. Frustrated
  total internal reflection through the plate yields a contact-pressure
  footprint whose asymmetry encodes camber and toe. A line laser
  supervises tread-depth regression at training time only, so inference
  is RGB-only. Wear and alignment are coupled by a physics-consistency
  loss derived from the brush tyre model, which additionally enables a
  diagnostic distinguishing recent from chronic misalignment.
keywords:
  - computer-vision
  - tyre-inspection
  - tire-wear
  - wheel-alignment
  - vehicle-safety
  - frustrated-total-internal-reflection
  - physics-informed-machine-learning
  - deep-learning
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-08-09'
